Feature: Refactored PySpark Sales KPI Pipeline with Classes and Functions

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog schema "purgo_playground" contains tables:
      | Table Name                  | Required Columns                                      |
      | product_data                | product_id:string, product_name:string, market_segment:string |
      | product_sales_data          | transaction_id:string, sales_product_id:string, sales_amount:bigint, sales_date:date |
      | product_marketshare_data    | ms_product_id:string, market_share_pct:double         |
    And the output table "sales_kpi" exists or will be created with columns:
      | sales_year:int | sales_product_id:string | product_name:string | market_segment:string | total_sales:bigint | prev_year_sales:bigint | yoy_growth_pct:double | avg_market_share:double | market_penetration_flag:string | sales_rank:int |
    And the Spark session is configured with "spark.sql.shuffle.partitions" set to 200

  Scenario: Happy path - All required data present and valid
    Given product_data contains products with valid product_id, product_name, and market_segment
    And product_sales_data contains sales transactions with non-null sales_amount and valid sales_date
    And product_marketshare_data contains market share records for products
    When the pipeline is executed using refactored classes and functions
    Then the output table "sales_kpi" contains KPIs for each product per year with columns:
      | sales_year | sales_product_id | product_name | market_segment | total_sales | prev_year_sales | yoy_growth_pct | avg_market_share | market_penetration_flag | sales_rank |
    And total_sales is the sum of sales_amount per product per year
    And prev_year_sales is the total_sales for the previous year for the same product (or null if not available)
    And yoy_growth_pct is ((total_sales - prev_year_sales) / prev_year_sales) * 100, rounded to 2 decimals (or null if prev_year_sales is null)
    And avg_market_share is the average of market_share_pct per product per year, rounded to 2 decimals
    And market_penetration_flag is "High" if avg_market_share > 25, "Medium" if avg_market_share between 10 and 25, "Low" if avg_market_share < 10
    And sales_rank is the row_number of the product by total_sales descending per year

  Scenario Outline: Error - Missing required columns in input tables
    Given <table_name> is missing required column <missing_column>
    When the pipeline is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Missing required column <missing_column> in <table_name>"

    Examples:
      | table_name                 | missing_column      |
      | product_data               | product_id          |
      | product_data               | product_name        |
      | product_data               | market_segment      |
      | product_sales_data         | sales_product_id    |
      | product_sales_data         | sales_amount        |
      | product_sales_data         | sales_date          |
      | product_marketshare_data   | ms_product_id       |
      | product_marketshare_data   | market_share_pct    |

  Scenario Outline: Error - Null or invalid data types in required fields
    Given <table_name> contains rows where <column> is null or not of type <expected_type>
    When the pipeline is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Invalid or null value in <column> of <table_name>"

    Examples:
      | table_name                 | column             | expected_type |
      | product_data               | product_id         | string        |
      | product_sales_data         | sales_product_id   | string        |
      | product_sales_data         | sales_amount       | bigint        |
      | product_sales_data         | sales_date         | date          |
      | product_marketshare_data   | ms_product_id      | string        |
      | product_marketshare_data   | market_share_pct   | double        |

  Scenario: Error - Duplicate product_id in product_data
    Given product_data contains duplicate product_id values
    When the pipeline is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Duplicate product_id found in product_data"

  Scenario: Error - Duplicate transaction_id in product_sales_data
    Given product_sales_data contains duplicate transaction_id values
    When the pipeline is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Duplicate transaction_id found in product_sales_data"

  Scenario Outline: Error - Data type mismatch in input tables
    Given <table_name> has column <column> with incorrect type <actual_type> (expected <expected_type>)
    When the pipeline is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Type mismatch for <column> in <table_name>: expected <expected_type>, got <actual_type>"

    Examples:
      | table_name                 | column             | actual_type | expected_type |
      | product_data               | product_id         | int         | string        |
      | product_sales_data         | sales_amount       | string      | bigint        |
      | product_marketshare_data   | market_share_pct   | string      | double        |

  Scenario: Error - Output table schema mismatch
    Given the output table "sales_kpi" exists with columns not matching the expected schema
    When the pipeline attempts to write results
    Then an error is raised with message "Output table sales_kpi schema mismatch"

  Scenario: Error - Write failure to output table
    Given the output table "sales_kpi" is not writable due to permissions or other issues
    When the pipeline attempts to write results
    Then an error is raised with message "Failed to write to output table sales_kpi"

  Scenario Outline: KPI calculation edge cases
    Given product_sales_data contains sales for <product_id> in <year> and <prev_year>
    And product_marketshare_data contains market_share_pct for <product_id>
    When the pipeline is executed
    Then the output for <product_id> in <year> has:
      | total_sales = <total_sales> |
      | prev_year_sales = <prev_year_sales> |
      | yoy_growth_pct = <yoy_growth_pct> |
      | avg_market_share = <avg_market_share> |
      | market_penetration_flag = <penetration_flag> |
      | sales_rank = <sales_rank> |

    Examples:
      | product_id | year | prev_year | total_sales | prev_year_sales | yoy_growth_pct | avg_market_share | penetration_flag | sales_rank |
      | P001       | 2023 | 2022      | 10000       | 8000            | 25.00          | 30.00            | High            | 1          |
      | P002       | 2023 | 2022      | 5000        | 5000            | 0.00           | 15.00            | Medium          | 2          |
      | P003       | 2023 | null      | 2000        | null            | null           | 8.00             | Low             | 3          |

  Scenario: Error - No sales data for a product in a year
    Given product_sales_data does not contain sales for product_id P004 in year 2023
    When the pipeline is executed
    Then the output does not contain a row for product_id P004 in year 2023

  Scenario: Error - No market share data for a product
    Given product_marketshare_data does not contain market_share_pct for product_id P005
    When the pipeline is executed
    Then avg_market_share is null and market_penetration_flag is "Low" for product_id P005

  Scenario: Error - Null prev_year_sales for first year
    Given product_sales_data contains sales for product_id P006 only in year 2022
    When the pipeline is executed
    Then prev_year_sales and yoy_growth_pct are null for product_id P006 in year 2022

  Scenario: Error - Multiple market_share_pct records per product per year
    Given product_marketshare_data contains multiple market_share_pct records for product_id P007 in year 2023
    When the pipeline is executed
    Then avg_market_share is the average of all market_share_pct values for product_id P007 in year 2023

  Scenario: Error - Display function not supported outside Databricks
    Given the pipeline is executed outside Databricks environment
    When the display function is called
    Then an error is raised with message "display function not supported outside Databricks"

  Scenario: Refactored pipeline uses classes and functions
    Given the pipeline code is refactored into reusable classes and functions
    When the pipeline is executed
    Then the output matches the results of the original script logic

# END
